<!--
  modules/xcos/pom.xml — Stage 2-f Task 5 module POM (Wave E, the FINAL
  wave) (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2f-remaining-modules.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/xcos -am package from
  the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/xcos/pom.xml package). Ant
  (modules/xcos/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains the real build; nothing
  here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. The second-largest module in the whole reactor (271
  source files — behind only gui's 351, Wave C) and the last of Wave E.
  Listed third (after scinotes, preferences) in the parent's <modules>; it
  depends on neither of this wave's other two modules, only on
  core/graph/gui/helptools/javasci/types (all migrated by earlier waves)
  plus action_binding/commons/localization.

  THIS IS THE MODULE THE Implementation-Version RULE EXISTS FOR.
  modules/localization/pom.xml's <build> comment (Stage 2-a, the very first
  POM in this whole campaign) named xcos BY NAME as "the actual reader this
  exists to satisfy" — and here it is. Two call sites read the per-package
  manifest section AT RUNTIME and stamp the result into every saved .xcos
  diagram file:
    - io/writer/CustomWriter.java:121 — inside `if (kind == Kind.DIAGRAM)`,
      `Package.getPackage("org.scilab.modules.xcos")` then
      `.getSpecificationVersion()` / `.getImplementationVersion()`, written
      as an XML comment at the top of the diagram's XML serialization.
    - io/codec/XcosDiagramCodec.java:304-305 — the same
      Package.getPackage(...).getSpecificationVersion()/
      .getImplementationVersion() pair, fed to `trace(...)` inside
      beforeEncode(), the mxCodec hook that runs for every encoded diagram
      object.
  Both resolve via java.lang.Package, which the JVM populates from the
  per-package manifest section named `Name: org/scilab/modules/xcos/` in
  whichever jar org.scilab.modules.xcos.* classes were loaded from —
  EXACTLY the section this POM's <manifestFile> fragment (below) supplies.
  If that section were absent, or present without an Implementation-Version
  attribute, getImplementationVersion() returns null (documented
  java.lang.Package behavior) and every diagram saved by a Maven-built xcos
  would silently carry the literal text "null" where a version stamp
  belongs — a real behavioral regression the build-parity harness CANNOT
  see: parity/fingerprint.py's normalize_manifest strips the
  Implementation-Version line from BOTH sides (Ant's live DSTAMP/TSTAMP
  value and this POM's frozen literal alike) before comparing, precisely so
  a stable rebuild doesn't fail parity on a timestamp — so "parity is green"
  and "getImplementationVersion() returns null" are BOTH possible
  simultaneously, and only reading the actual runtime consumer (as this
  comment does) tells them apart. VERIFIED PRESENT in the built jar below —
  see the Stage 2-f Task 5 report for the `unzip -p .../org.scilab.modules.
  xcos.jar META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` transcript of the actual built artifact.

  A macOS/BSD-sed TOOL BUG affects maven-module-deps.sh's section [1] raw
  output here too (self-referencing org.scilab.modules.xcos.* imports —
  actions, block, configuration, explorer, graph, io, link, modelica,
  palette, port, preferences, utils and their sub-packages — leak in
  unfiltered instead of being excluded). See modules/scinotes/pom.xml's
  header comment for the full root cause; not repeated here. Every
  dependency below was cross-checked against a corrected, self-reference-
  free pass (POSIX bracket classes instead of the tool's `\s`), not the raw
  script output alone.

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh xcos, 271 files; self-reference
  noise removed per modules/scinotes/pom.xml's header comment):
    [1] imports resolve to NINE reactor dependencies, all below (all already
        migrated by earlier waves): action_binding ({,highlevel.}
        ScilabInterpreterManagement, incl. three static-imported methods),
        commons ({,gui,xml}.*, incl. a static import of commons.OS), core
        (Scilab), graph (ScilabComponent, ScilabGraph, actions.*,
        actions.base.*, event.ArrowKeyListener, io.{ScilabGraphCodec,
        ScilabObjectCodec}, utils.*), gui (a wide surface: bridge.*,
        checkboxmenuitem, contextmenu, events.callback, filechooser, menu,
        menubar, menuitem, messagebox{,.ScilabModalDialog}, tab,
        tabfactory, textbox, toolbar, utils), helptools (image.
        XcosImageConverter — see "THE HELPTOOLS / XCOS MUTUAL REFERENCE"
        below), javasci (JavasciException, Scilab), localization (Messages),
        types (Boolean, Double, Integer, IntegerTypeEnum, List, MList,
        String, TList, Type, TypeEnum).
    [2] reflection targets — NONE (the tool's own verdict, confirmed by an
        independent `grep -rn 'Class\.forName\|loadClass('` sweep of all 271
        files: zero hits — xcos is a reflection TARGET for other modules
        [helptools' XcosDelegates finding, graph's earlier javadoc-only
        near-miss] but never a reflection SOURCE itself).
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import — every org.scilab.modules.*
        name is already covered by the nine reactor dependencies above,
        nothing new. The vendored-jar entries (com.mxgraph.*,
        javax.xml.bind{,.annotation}.*, org.apache.batik.transcoder{,.image}.*,
        org.apache.lucene.*, org.flexdock.{docking.activation,
        plaf.common.border}.*) are handled below, each verified per-file
        against this module's OWN source, not merely copied from the tool's
        list. javax.annotation.Generated does NOT appear anywhere in this
        module (confirmed: `grep -rln "javax.annotation" modules/xcos/src/
        java` is empty) — xcos has no JFlex-generated lexer, unlike
        scinotes/helptools/graphic_objects, so javax.annotation-api is
        correctly NOT a dependency here.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml (confirmed again in the
  Ant-built jar's manifest: Class-Path is the literal, never-interpolated
  string "${manifest.class-path}").

  THE HELPTOOLS / XCOS MUTUAL REFERENCE, CLOSING THE LOOP. modules/helptools/
  pom.xml's header comment documents a reflection target RULED OUT:
  helptools' image/XcosImageConverter.java reaches
  `org.scilab.modules.xcos.utils.XcosDelegates` only via
  Class.forName(...), specifically to avoid a hard compile-time dependency
  on xcos (which depends on helptools directly — a hard edge the other way
  would cycle the reactor). Landing here confirms the OTHER half: xcos's own
  utils/XcosDelegates.java:24 imports
  `org.scilab.modules.helptools.image.XcosImageConverter` with a plain,
  ordinary `import` statement — mentioned only in a `@see {@link
  XcosImageConverter}` javadoc tag in this file (convertToPNG's actual body
  calls com.mxgraph.util.mxCellRenderer directly, not XcosImageConverter),
  but a plain unused-in-code import is still real Java source that requires
  the package to resolve at compile time (javac errors on an unresolvable
  import regardless of whether the imported name is later referenced) — so
  `helptools` is a genuine dependency here for this reason alone, independent
  of the image-conversion delegation itself.

  EXTENDS-CHAIN CHECKS, TO RULE OUT TRANSITIVE VENDORED DEPENDENCIES FROM
  graph. xcos subclasses graph extensively (XcosDiagram extends ScilabGraph;
  GraphComponent/PaletteComponent extend ScilabComponent; XcosDiagramCodec
  extends ScilabGraphCodec; XcosConstants extends ScilabGraphConstants; ~15
  action classes extend graph's DefaultAction). modules/graph/pom.xml
  carries FOUR vendored jars (jgraphx, batik-all, jeuclid-core, jlatexmath);
  Maven system-scope dependencies are never transitive, so depending on
  graph's jar does not hand any of those to xcos automatically — but if
  DefaultAction or ScilabGraph exposed a jeuclid/jlatexmath type in a
  signature xcos touches, xcos would need that jar too, independent of
  transitivity. Checked directly: DefaultAction's and ScilabGraph's own
  import lists (modules/graph/src/java/org/scilab/modules/graph/actions/
  base/DefaultAction.java, .../ScilabGraph.java) resolve entirely to
  java.*/javax.swing (JDK), commons/gui/graph (reactor, already covered),
  and com.mxgraph.* (already needed here directly, see below) — no
  net.sourceforge.jeuclid or org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath anywhere in either
  chain. jeuclid-core and jlatexmath are correctly NOT dependencies of this
  module.

  JGRAPHX — com.mxgraph.{io,model,swing{,.handler,.util},util,view}.* across
  this module's block/graph/io/link/palette/port packages (the diagram model
  and Swing canvas xcos is built on). SAME COORDINATE, SAME EVIDENCE AS
  modules/graph/pom.xml (cross-referenced, not restated — that file's header
  comment cites the jar's own OSGi manifest: Bundle-SymbolicName: com.mxgraph,
  Vendor: JGraph Ltd, Bundle-Version: 2.1.0.7). Also independently needed
  here regardless of the graph dependency: xcos imports twice as many
  com.mxgraph.* names directly as graph does.

  BATIK — org.apache.batik.transcoder{,.image}.{TranscoderException,
  TranscoderInput, TranscoderOutput, ImageTranscoder} — utils/
  ImageIconTranscoder.java (an SVG-to-icon transcoder) and palette/model/
  PaletteBlock.java. SAME COORDINATE AS modules/helptools/pom.xml and
  modules/graph/pom.xml (cross-referenced, not restated).

  THE LUCENE PAIR, INCLUDING A REAL Ant-CLASSPATH ALIAS. palette/
  {PaletteSearcher,PaletteIndexer,PaletteSearchManager}.java import
  org.apache.lucene.{analysis.{,standard.StandardAnalyzer},
  document.{Document,Field,StringField,TextField},
  index.{DirectoryReader,IndexReader,IndexWriter,IndexWriterConfig},
  search.{IndexSearcher,Query,ScoreDoc,TopDocs},
  store.ByteBuffersDirectory} plus
  queryparser.flexible.{core.QueryNodeException,
  standard.StandardQueryParser} — Xcos's block/palette search index.
  scilab-lib.properties (generated from scilab-lib.properties.in) sets BOTH
  `lucene-core.jar` AND `lucene-analyzers-common.jar` to the SAME absolute
  path, thirdparty/lucene-core-9.10.0.jar — confirmed by reading the
  generated properties file directly, and explained by fetch-thirdparty.sh:
  247's own comment, `ln -sf lucene-core-9.10.0.jar
  "$TP/lucene-analyzers-common-9.10.0.jar"   # class moved in Lucene 9`:
  org.apache.lucene.analysis.standard.StandardAnalyzer, split into its own
  lucene-analyzers-common artifact in older Lucene, was folded back into
  lucene-core itself as of Lucene 9 — confirmed directly, `unzip -l
  thirdparty/lucene-core-9.10.0.jar` lists
  org/apache/lucene/analysis/standard/StandardAnalyzer.class alongside
  org/apache/lucene/{document,index,store}/*.class. Ant's compile.classpath
  (build.incl.xml:88-89) therefore puts the SAME physical file on the
  classpath under two different property names; reproduced here as ONE
  dependency (org.apache.lucene:lucene-core:9.10.0) rather than two
  <dependency> entries pointing at identical bytes — javac resolves a class
  from whichever classpath entry supplies it first, so a duplicate
  <systemPath> entry for the same file would be inert, not more faithful.
  lucene-queryparser-9.10.0.jar is a genuinely separate file (`unzip -l`
  confirms org/apache/lucene/queryparser/flexible/{core,standard}/*.class
  live only there), added as its own dependency below. Both real Maven
  Central coordinates (org.apache.lucene), high confidence — well-known
  groupId, and the jars' own internal timestamps (2024-02-14) line up with
  Lucene 9.10.0's real release date.

  JAXB-API — javax.xml.bind.{JAXBContext, JAXBElement, JAXBException,
  Marshaller, Unmarshaller} and javax.xml.bind.annotation.{XmlAccessType,
  XmlAccessorType, XmlAttribute, XmlElement, XmlElementDecl, XmlElementRef,
  XmlElementRefs, XmlElements, XmlRegistry, XmlRootElement, XmlSchemaType,
  XmlSeeAlso, XmlTransient, XmlType} — the modelica/ and configuration/model/
  JAXB-annotated data-binding classes (22 files: ModelicaController,
  Modelica, the modelica.model.* value classes and their ObjectFactory,
  configuration.model.{SettingType,DocumentType,ObjectFactory}, and the
  palette.model.* value classes and their ObjectFactory). Removed from the
  JDK at Java 11 (the exact class of gap this tool's header names by name —
  javax.xml.bind is in its always-report list). Real, well-known Maven
  Central coordinate (javax.xml.bind:jaxb-api), only the API is needed at
  compile time (build.incl.xml's shared classpath puts ONLY jaxb-api.jar
  there, not the separate jaxb-impl/jaxb-runtime jars also vendored under
  thirdparty/ — those are runtime-only implementation classes, confirmed
  against build.incl.xml:105, a single `${jaxb-api.jar}` pathelement and
  nothing else naming jaxb).

  FLEXDOCK — org.flexdock.docking.activation.ActiveDockableTracker
  (ViewPortTab.java, XcosTab.java) and org.flexdock.plaf.common.border.
  ShadowBorder (palette/view/PaletteBlockView.java). SAME COORDINATE AS
  modules/commons/pom.xml and modules/gui/pom.xml (cross-referenced, not
  restated) — a different pair of flexdock sub-packages than those two
  modules use, same jar, verified per-class: `unzip -l thirdparty/
  flexdock-1.2.5.jar` lists both org/flexdock/docking/activation/
  ActiveDockableTracker.class and org/flexdock/plaf/common/border/
  ShadowBorder.class.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>xcos</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:19 <property name="library.title" value="Modeler and simulator for hybrid systems"/> -->
  <name>Modeler and simulator for hybrid systems</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.action_binding.highlevel.
         ScilabInterpreterManagement, also via static imports of
         asynchronousScilabExec/buildCall/synchronousScilabExec. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>action_binding</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.{CommonFileUtils, ScilabCommons,
         ScilabConstants, gui.{FindIconHelper,ScilabLAF}, xml.*}, also via a
         static import of commons.OS. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.core.Scilab. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>core</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.graph.* — ScilabComponent, ScilabGraph,
         actions.*, actions.base.* (the base xcos's own ~15 action classes
         extend — see this file's header comment, "EXTENDS-CHAIN CHECKS"),
         event.ArrowKeyListener, io.{ScilabGraphCodec,ScilabObjectCodec},
         utils.*. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>graph</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.gui.* — bridge.{contextmenu,filechooser,menu,
         menubar,menuitem,tab,toolbar,window}, checkboxmenuitem,
         contextmenu, events.callback, filechooser, menu, menubar, menuitem,
         messagebox{,.ScilabModalDialog}, tab, tabfactory, textbox, toolbar,
         utils. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>gui</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.helptools.image.XcosImageConverter —
         utils/XcosDelegates.java. See this file's header comment, "THE
         HELPTOOLS / XCOS MUTUAL REFERENCE". -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>helptools</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.javasci.{JavasciException, Scilab}. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>javasci</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages — the ordinary
         reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every module. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.types.{Boolean, Double, Integer,
         IntegerTypeEnum, List, MList, String, TList, Type, TypeEnum} — the
         block/port data-type model. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>types</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- JGRAPHX — see this file's header comment for the coordinate
         evidence (cross-referenced from modules/graph/pom.xml, not
         restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.mxgraph</groupId>
      <artifactId>jgraphx</artifactId>
      <version>2.1.0.7</version>
      <scope>system</scope>
      <systemPath>${project.basedir}/../../thirdparty/jgraphx-2.1.0.7.jar</systemPath>
    </dependency>
    <!-- BATIK — see this file's header comment (cross-referenced from
         modules/helptools/pom.xml and modules/graph/pom.xml, not
         restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>batik-all</artifactId>
      <version>1.17</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- LUCENE-CORE — covers BOTH org.apache.lucene.{document,index,store}.*
         AND org.apache.lucene.analysis.standard.StandardAnalyzer (folded
         into lucene-core as of Lucene 9; Ant's own lucene-analyzers-common.jar
         property resolves to this identical file). See this file's header
         comment, "THE LUCENE PAIR", for the full alias evidence. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.lucene</groupId>
      <artifactId>lucene-core</artifactId>
      <version>9.10.0</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- LUCENE-QUERYPARSER — org.apache.lucene.queryparser.flexible.
         {core.QueryNodeException, standard.StandardQueryParser}, a
         genuinely separate jar from lucene-core (see this file's header
         comment). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.lucene</groupId>
      <artifactId>lucene-queryparser</artifactId>
      <version>9.10.0</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- JAXB-API — javax.xml.bind{,.annotation}.* across the modelica/ and
         configuration/model/ data-binding classes. Removed from the JDK at
         Java 11; only the API jar is on Ant's shared compile classpath (not
         the separate jaxb-impl/jaxb-runtime implementation jars also
         vendored under thirdparty/ — see this file's header comment). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>javax.xml.bind</groupId>
      <artifactId>jaxb-api</artifactId>
      <version>2.3.1</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- FLEXDOCK — org.flexdock.docking.activation.ActiveDockableTracker,
         org.flexdock.plaf.common.border.ShadowBorder. SAME COORDINATE AS
         modules/commons/pom.xml and modules/gui/pom.xml (cross-referenced,
         not restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.flexdock</groupId>
      <artifactId>flexdock</artifactId>
      <version>1.2.5</version>
      <scope>system</scope>
      <systemPath>${project.basedir}/../../thirdparty/flexdock-1.2.5.jar</systemPath>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/xcos/jar/org.scilab.modules.xcos.jar
                 META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped: Specification-Vendor
                 and Implementation-Vendor both carry the double-mangled
                 "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
                 fuller comment for the mechanism.

                 IMPLEMENTATION-VERSION IS NOT OPTIONAL HERE — see this
                 file's header comment, "THIS IS THE MODULE THE
                 Implementation-Version RULE EXISTS FOR", for the two actual
                 runtime call sites (CustomWriter.java:121,
                 XcosDiagramCodec.java:304-305) that read this exact
                 section's Implementation-Version attribute via
                 java.lang.Package at runtime and stamp the result into
                 every saved .xcos diagram file. Present below, frozen at
                 the literal "00000000 0000", positioned between
                 Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor exactly
                 where Ant places it (Ant's live value there today:
                 "20260719 1729", a DSTAMP/TSTAMP pair) — confirmed in the
                 BUILT Maven jar, not merely in this source fragment, per
                 the Stage 2-f Task 5 report. -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
